== Installation ==

1. Upload the plugin folder to the `/wp-content/plugins/` directory.
2. Activate the plugin through the 'Plugins' menu in WordPress.
3. Start editing a post or page where you want to add footnotes.
4. Locate the metabox "CM Footnotes - Definitions" and add the definitions themselves.
5. Insert shortcodes with relevant definition IDs to the needed places in the content.
6. Save the changes in the post/page.

Note: You must have a call to wp_head() in your template in order for the footnote js and css to work properly. If your theme does not support this you will need to link to these files manually in your theme (not recommended).

